1:Nana Shiraishi
2:...Ah! You're here!
3:Just as I'm about to have a nice nap today, Nana Shiraishi suddenly calls me and says she has something to discuss with me. She sounds a little anxious on the phone, so I fight my sleepiness and go to the café where we agreed to meet.
4:player
5:Do you need me to help you with anything urgently?
6:Well... what do you think about me?
7:Why are you suddenly asking me that? Is it for some kind of survey assignment?
8:No, it's not that. Just answer my question first.
9:Let me think... You're carefree, can hit it off with anyone right away, and love to help others. As a whole, you're a nice person, but sometimes you move before you think, which makes you a little reckless.
10:Oh, and you're afraid of dogs.
11:Umm... you don't have to mention my weakness. Now comment on things other than my personality, such as my appearance.
12:Well, you definitely look cute.
13:Ohhh! H-How cute would you say I look?!
14:Do you think I look cute enough that it wouldn't be weird if I'm dating someone?!
15:Please control your emotions, my friend... With your looks, it wouldn't be difficult for you to find a boyfriend.
16:Hehe! So you also think that too.
17:Please also control your expressions. You're starting to look really proud even though I barely praised you.
18:You're exaggerating things. Oh, anyway... umm, would you be willing to go on a date with me?
19:Oh, so you want to ask me to play with you. You could have just asked me directly instead of being so indirect about it.
20:I'm not asking you to go out and play with me. I'm asking you out on a date... the type of date that couples go on!
21:The type of date... that couples go on?
22:My first reaction after hearing this abrupt invitation is that this is a prank Nana Shiraishi is playing on me. I look around but don't see anyone taking photos discreetly. Nana Shiraishi, on the other hand, starts to blush shyly, so I start to believe that she's being serious about this.
23:In that case, I will...
24:Say yes
25:Say no
26:I guess I can...
27:You seem kinda reluctant... but this is great! I knew you would say yes.
28:Don't get so happy so soon. Since you're asking me out on a date so suddenly, can you tell me what's happened? I won't believe you if you tell me this is just a whim.
29:Umm... you're usually quite slow, so why are you so astute today?
30:Tell me now, or I'm going to change my mind.
31:No, no, no! Don't do that! I'll tell you now. It's like this. When I was chatting with my classmates a few days ago...
32:I understand what you're saying, but I'm going to turn you down!
33:Eh... Eh?!!! Don't you want to go on a date with me, your cute, sexy, and charming senpai?
34:Where did that part about being sexy and charming come from...? This request is too sudden, even if it's coming from my cute, sexy, and charming senpai. There's no way I can agree to it just like that.
35:Th-Then what will it take for you to say yes?
36:You need to tell me what's happened at the very least. I won't believe you if you tell me this is just a whim.
37:Fine then... It's like this. When I was chatting with my classmates a few days ago...
38:Jill
39:Nana, are you really not going to go sing karaoke with us next weekend? For once, that new handsome member of the basketball team will be coming, and I heard that he likes lively, sporty girls. It would be such a shame if you missed this opportunity!

41:I-I'll pass. I'm busy next weekend, Jill, enjoy yourself with the others.
42:Sigh, you always make an excuse to run away whenever I want to introduce some guys to you. You won't be young forever, Nana. Why aren't you interested in falling in love with anyone?
43:Look at how full my daily schedule is, and I even help sports clubs on the weekends every now and then. I don't have any time to fall in love. In fact, I might as well say that my lover is this school!
44:Don't try to change the subject. I'm serious here. As they say, the time you have for love is like water in a sponge - you will have it while you squeeze. Even if you aren't thinking of dating anyone right now, it wouldn't hurt to get to know more guys. But you don't seem to have any intention of doing that at all. Don't tell me...
45:Is it possible that you're in a secret relationship and won't join our gatherings because your boyfriend won't let you?
46:What on earth are you saying? I really am just too busy.
48:Since when did such an organization exist? Have you registered it with the vice president yet...?
49:Student A
50:Hehe, it's possible that you really haven't noticed, Jill. I often see Nana hanging out with someone I don't know recently, and that person doesn't look like a student of our school.
51:Student B
52:Now that you mention it... A few days ago, I saw Nana holding hands with someone I don't know while they were being chased through the streets by Yuzu and an Alaskan. Is it possible that we're talking about the same person?
53:Y-You were mistaken. We weren't holding hands...
54:Student C
55:Ah! Could this person be the junior that Nana is always talking about?
56:What?! That's not...
57:I see... So even my love radar malfunctions sometimes. I'm really impressed, Nana. You managed to hide everything so well. Come on, who is this person? How did you meet? When did you start dating?!
58:I-It's not what you think...
59:The more you try to explain, the more it sounds like you're trying to cover things up, which means you're admitting that it's true. We're all smart people here, so it won't look good if you keep trying to hide it from us, Nana.
60:I'm going on a date with my boyfriend this weekend, so why don't you join us with your boyfriend? I want to see the person you're so infatuated with that you're completely uninterested in the handsome guys I've tried to introduce to you. It's settled then!
61:W-Wait! Jill, let me explain!
62:Okay, I understand everything now. If it's just a misunderstanding, then why didn't you explain things clearly at that time instead of making someone like me pretend to be your boyfriend?
63:You have a point... but I have a reason for doing this.
64:Jill is always trying to help me find a boyfriend, and she's so enthusiastic about it. I've rejected her so many times that I'm starting to feel bad about it. Since she already misunderstood, I think this is an opportunity to make her really think that I'm in a relationship, and then she'll stop trying to introduce guys to me.
65:I see, you kinda make some sense.
66:I remember seeing it mentioned in the news that some people deliberately pay others to pretend to be their lover and return home with them to avoid being pressured into marriage by their elders and to have some peace and quiet. Nana Shiraishi wants to do something similar to deal with her overly enthusiastic classmate.
67:Please! I can only ask you, my most trustworthy junior, to help me with this. Please help me!
68:...Fine then. I'll do my best to help you, but you'll need to deal with the mess if they see through our act.
69:Everything will be alright as long as you're willing to help me! Thanks a lot! This meal is on me, so order whatever you want to eat or drink... oh, umm, m-maybe you can go easy on me because my pocket money is running a little low recently...
70:It's just a small favor, so you don't have to make such a big deal out of it. Let's plan what we'll do on the date before the weekend, or else it'll be embarrassing if they see through our act immediately.
71:Seeing Nana Shiraishi beg me so pitifully to help her, as her "most trustworthy junior," I can't really just ignore her plea.
72:It's also true that the rumors that made her classmates think she was in a relationship are also related to me in some way.
73:On the day of our date, I deliberately get up earlier than usual to make myself look more presentable and arrive at the agreed meeting place early. After playing with the little stray cat by the road for a while, I see Nana Shiraishi walking over with a bag on her back.
74:Eh? This sure is rare. You're actually here before me.
75:Aren't we going on a date today? I shouldn't make you wait for me.
76:Hehe, good initiative. I hope you haven't been waiting for too long though. Don't tell me... Did you look forward to today's date so much that you set up a tent somewhere nearby and slept here?
77:No way! I only left home about half an hour early. So? Are you feeling confident about today's date?
78:Relax! I've made a lot of preparations for today. We can definitely pull it off!
79:???
80:Pull what off?
81:Eek... G-Good morning, Jill. When did you guys get here?
82:When you were shouting loudly with a lot of momentum about being able to pull something off.
83:Oh no... our date plan has fallen through before we've even started.
84:Nana, don't tell me you...
85:Wh-What are you trying to say...?
86:In addition to the double date, have you also made other arrangements, such as secret and private plans for tonight? Ehehe, I'm right, aren't I?
87:A-Ahahaha... so that's what you mean. What I meant was that I wanted to enjoy today's date. That's all, so please don't make random guesses or make such a sleazy grin, Jill.
88:Okay, okay. I'll stop teasing you. Anyway, so is this the one I've heard so much about?
89:Nice to meet you, I'm {var:player_nickname}.
90:Whoa, what a formal greeting. You don't need to be so reserved. Just call me Jill like Nana. The person next to me is my boyfriend, of course.
91:What's his name? You're Jill, so don't tell me he's called Jack.
92:Jack
93:Huh? Are you telepathic or something? How did know that my name is Jack?
94:...That's really his name?!
95:Okay, we're done with the introductions. Let's go to the cinema like we planned.
96:Let's go, {var:player_nickname}.
97:...Oh, okay.
98:Why did you look at me so sluggishly just then? Were you thinking about something?
99:(whisper) I'm so used to hearing you call me your junior that it took me a moment to realize you were talking to me.
100:(whisper) I see. Then should I call you something else to make it more obvious that I'm talking to you like "darling" or something?
101:(whisper) Urgh... Hearing that is making the hairs on the back of my hands stand up.
102:(whisper) Hehe, are you serious? I don't believe you, darling...
103:(whisper) If you're going to do this, then two can play this game.
104:Huh?!
105:Nana Shiraishi jumps away from me quickly like a frightened cat the moment I hold her hand, catching the attention of Jill, who is walking in front of us. She turns around and squints at Nana Shiraishi with confusion.
106:Hmm? What is it, Nana?
107:Nothing, maybe my hand was a little cold today, so I gave her a fright when I held her hand.
108:Y-Yes, why is your hand so cold? I bet you haven't been exercising properly recently. Give me your hands so I can rub them and warm them up for you.
109:Okay... (whisper) Calm down. Isn't it normal for couples to hold hands? Don't make a fuss over it.
110:Aha... (whisper) You're right... but aren't you also blushing right now?
111:(whisper) I'm blushing because of something else...
112:After all, she only said she would rub my hands, not that she would hold them and breathe on them to warm them up like what's happening right now.
113:Nana, are there any other movies you wanna watch? If there aren't any, we'll watch "A Romantic Holiday" like we planned.
114:Let's watch that. I have some discount vouchers, so I'll buy the tickets.
115:(whisper) I just took a look at this and saw that it's a chick flick. So you like this type of movie?
116:(whisper) To be honest, I'm not that interested, but isn't this the right type of movie to watch on a date?
117:...Eh? A new Masked Hero movie is playing here?! Oh, it's a test screening. No wonder I didn't know about it.
118:I remember that you love Masked Hero, Nana. Didn't you also show off your villain-fighting skills on the stage of a hero show when you were little?
119:Hehe, that was the first time I fought against the villains. It's such a pity that I can't fight the villains on the stage anymore now even if I watch a hero show.
120:Nana, have you got the tickets?
121:Oh, sorry about that. It'll just be a little longer.
122:Didn't you want to watch the Masked Hero movie?
123:I'll come back and watch it with my little brother later. After all, that little kid loves the masked heroes too. It's just such a shame because you can get a special full-color poster if you watch it today.
124:I see...
125:Recommend watching the chick flick
126:Propose to watch the live-action hero movie
127:It's a little strange for a couple to watch a live-action hero movie like Masked Hero on a date. Like what Nana Shiraishi said, the right movie to watch at a time like this is a chick flick, so we'll watch "A Romantic Holiday" together as planned...
128:Hmm.. Mmm...
129:That was close. I almost yawned out loud. This movie's pace is so slow that I'm getting sleepy.
130:Zzz... Zzz...
131:...Geez, Nana Shiraishi has beaten me to it and fallen asleep at some point. I can even hear the faint sound of her breathing while asleep. Seeing that she is sleeping so soundly, I pinch the back of her hand gently.
132:Ouch, that hurts...
133:Seeing that Nana Shiraishi is now awake and about to say something, I quickly place my finger against her lips to remind her to stay quiet. After that, I grab my phone, make it as dim as it can get, and write a text message for her.
134:(Text Message) You shouldn't really fall asleep even if the movie is really boring! They might realize something if we get so bored that we fall asleep instead of enjoying the romantic atmosphere.
135:Nana Shiraishi gets what I mean. She turns so that her back is facing Jill, then she also makes her phone as dim as it can get like me.
136:(Text Message) Oh no! I fell asleep just then. What should I do?!
137:(Text Message) Jill seems to be very focused on watching the movie, so she probably didn't notice that you fell asleep. The important thing is that you can't fall asleep again now!
138:(Text Message) Got it! Just like being stranded on a snowy mountain - you'll be a goner if you fall asleep!
139:(Text Message) Well, I couldn't go as far as to say that you'll be a goner...
140:(Text Message) Tsk, tsk, tsk. You don't understand. That's the mindset we need to survive until the end in today's challenge of pretending to be a couple!
141:(Text Message) I hope a certain someone who has already fallen asleep once will be able to remember this then.
142:(Text Message) I just let down my guard in a momentary lapse of concentration! Don't worry, I won't fall asleep again!
143:(Text Message) ...But if, if I accidentally fall asleep again, please don't leave me alone.
144:(Text Message) Then you better pray that I'll still be awake if that happens.
145:It doesn't take long before this "what if" situation happens. In just five minutes, I start to hear a familiar breathing sound next to me again...
146:...(whisper) I'm going to pinch you now.
147:Ouch!
148:Judging from how I need to pinch her every five minutes to keep her awake, I don't think I need to worry about falling asleep myself.
149:Hey, why do you always drool everywhere whenever we watch a romance movie together? And you don't respond either when I ask you to pass me a tissue.
150:Yaaaawn... This movie is too boring. I think it's already great that I could stay awake for the first five minutes of it.
151:I'm impressed with your patience, {var:player_nickname}. You actually managed to watch the whole thing without falling asleep. You have my respect.
152:I-It was okay. The movie does have a slow pace, but the story is quite well-written.
153:By the way, I'm surprised that you didn't fall asleep, Nana. You're always the first the fall asleep whenever we watch romance movies.
154:Well, I'm watching it with a special person today. Isn't that right, {var:player_nickname}?
155:Ouch... Ah, yes, yes, you're right...
156:This one pinch from Nana Shiraishi probably hurts more than all the pinches I gave her combined, but I can only endure the pain because she would have been able to sleep peacefully without any feelings of anxiety or pain if we noticed that Jack had fallen asleep sooner.
157:...I'm sorry, Jill, but I'm more interested in another movie. Can we watch that one instead while you watch this romance movie?
158:Eh? Th-That's not good, right? We agreed to watch the same movie together.
159:That's okay. {var:player_nickname}, which one do you want to watch?
160:I want to watch the new Masked Hero movie. I'm a diehard fan of this series.
161:I remember that Nana loves Masked Hero too. Bird of a flock fly together, huh? We'll watch the movies separately then.
162:I also want to watch the Masked Hero movie.
163:You get over here now! You better stay awake throughout the movie too. You'll be in trouble if you don't hand me a tissue when I'm crying!
164:And so, the two couples entered separate cinema rooms after having their tickets checked...
165:Junior, is this really okay? Even if we both like Masked Hero, wouldn't it be strange if a couple watches a live-action hero movie together? Are you sure Jill won't get suspicious?
166:There's nothing to worry about. A date is about doing something we both like to do or want to do, right? Think about it, if we're both not interested in that romance movie, or even fall asleep, then Jill would feel even more suspicious.
167:You have a point.
168:Also, don't forget to call me by my name during this time. I'm afraid you'll start calling me junior again after we finish the movie by habit.
169:Oh, right...
170:Although I try to comfort Nana Shiraishi by telling her not to overthink things, she still looks uneasy and keeps looking at the doors of the cinema room from time to time after sitting down. Fortunately, she is soon broken out of this uneasy state as the big screen lights up and she quickly focuses on the movie.
171:Voice on the Screen
172:You want me to retreat? Never! I'm here to protect the children's dreams! Final Judgment Form!
173:{var:player_nickname}, look! That's the ultimate form of the hero in this movie. It looks so cool, right?!
174:Yes, it is very cool. The seats are shaking really strongly, so you better be careful in case you fall off it.
175:As the story reaches its climax, Nana Shiraishi and the children around her get more and more excited. They cheer for the masked hero on the screen, giving the cinema room a lively atmosphere. The special seats designed for this 4D movie shake more and more violently as the battles get more and more intense, and I even start to wonder if I'm riding a roller coaster.
176:Ouch... my back hurts...
177:Let me make a correction. I feel like I'm on a roller coaster and getting a full-body massage at the same time. The seat shakes and vibrates from time to time, and the vibrations make me feel like I'm one of the villains on the screen getting beaten up and rolling on the floor...
178:The movie was great, and I got the full-color poster. I'm super satisfied now!
179:Hahaha, I'm glad that you're happy.
180:We're also finished over here. Hmm? {var:player_nickname}, why do you look a little tired?
181:I'm alright. I just feel a little too relaxed after getting a full-body massage.
182:You got to sit on massage chairs in your movie? That's so nice! We should have watched the Masked Hero movie too. Our one was so boring that I fell asleep. I would've slept more comfortably if we had massage chairs too.
183:How dare you even mention that?!
184:Umm... be careful. Your elbow is just a few centimeters away from my kidney...
185:It's almost time to have lunch. Is there anything you want to eat? I'll search for a suitable restaurant nearby.
186:You don't have to worry about that. I've got lunch sorted. Ta-da! I brought bento boxes.
187:Eh? You brought bento boxes?
188:It's an iron rule of shojo manga to prepare bento boxes when going out on a date!
189:Wow! You brought bento boxes for our date. That's so traditional. This doesn't even happen often in shojo manga now.
190:Eh, r-really?
191:That's right. But this is great. It looks like I asked the right person to go on a double date with us today. Ta-da, I also brought bento boxes! Nana, welcome to our big family of girls who go on dates the traditional way.
192:...Wow... Long live tradition! Jill!
193:Oh... you just found another companion. Are you really so happy that you're crying?
194:Ah, I'm starving. Don't just show me the food. Let's sit down and eat it.
195:I remember there's a nice park around here. Let's sit there and eat.
196:After arriving at the park and sitting down, I open the bento box Nana Shiraishi prepared for me and am impressed by what I see inside it.
197:Ohh?! The presentation is amazing, and it looks so delicious.
198:{var:player_nickname}, why are you acting like it's the first time you've seen Nana's bento boxes? Doesn't she usually make them for you? I remember that she always makes them for her little brother.
199:Well... she's always so busy, so I haven't been asking her to make them for me because I don't want her to work so hard. What's more, her bento boxes feel nicer and more delicious when I only get to eat them when we're on a date.
200:Oh? Are you saying that it isn't delicious if you eat it all the time?
201:I didn't say that. Let me try it first.
202:Hold on, don't be so impatient.
203:Umm... Nana, what are you...
204:I don't bring a bento box for you every day, so of course, I want to feed you the first bite. Come on, open your mouth. Ah...
205:I see! So you brought bento boxes because you wanted to act all lovey-dovey. We won't get in your way then. Jack and I will go over there, so you can be as lovey-dovey as you want.
206:...(whisper) I-Is it necessary to go so far...?
207:(whisper) Of course! Isn't this the classic development in shojo manga? Quickly, my arm is getting sore.
208:Let her feed you
209:Eat it yourself
210:O-Okay then... Ah...
211:Now that's a good boy. So why did you hesitate for so long? Is it because you're embarrassed about me feeding you in front of others?
212:More or less...
213:Hehe, you're finally starting to get embarrassed too. {var:player_nickname}, you've been acting the same as usual so far today, so I feel like I've lost because I'm the only one who has been getting nervous because of this date.
214:Is it necessary to be competitive over something like this...? Anyway, just feed me already. If I keep my mouth open for any longer, it'll get as sore as your arm. Ah...
215:Sure, here it comes, hehe...
216:...
217:A meatball slides smoothly across the left side of my face, leaving a trail of sauce behind.
218:S-Sorry, my hand slipped. Hehe...
219:...I hope the sauce mark on the right side of my face will be symmetrical with my left cheek.
220:Th-This is strange. Let me try again...
221:Stop, stop, stop! If you keep feeding me, my face will become a messy canvas before any food even gets in my mouth. Why are your hands shaking so badly? Could it be... are you also feeling embarrassed about feeding me?
222:Hahaha, there's no such thing! I'm just a little nervous because I've never fed anyone before.
223:You look quite sweaty, my friend.
224:Stop talking for now because you're distracting me. Phew... (whisper) Calm down, Nana Shiraishi. You can do something as simple as feeding someone. You don't need to get nervous or feel embarrassed...
225:Ah... (whisper) My lower jaw is starting to get sore.
226:...Now!
227:Huh?!
228:I finally managed to get my first bite of the food. It sure wasn't easy.
229:F-Forget it. I can eat it myself.
230:Oh? It's not such a big deal even if I feed you. That's so not cute. So why did you hesitate for so long? Is it because you're embarrassed about me feeding you in front of others?
231:You're being competitive about something strange again... but I'm really embarrassed about you feeding me, so I surrender. Now let me have a good taste of your cooking.
232:What should I try first... I know, I'll try this meatball.
233:Nom, nom, nom... Urgh?! Water, water...
234:{var:player_nickname}, did you choke on something?! Here, drink some water.
235:Glug... Relax, I didn't choke on anything. This meatball is so spicy.
236:Oops, I'm sorry, I forgot to tell you that the food I make is a little spicy.
237:A little spicy?
238:Everyone's constitution is different, and Nana Shiraishi and I should have quite a different idea of what we consider as being "a little spicy." I fan my tongue, which is still tingling painfully, and don't have the courage to keep eating the meatballs for now, so I reach out for the vegetables next to me with my chopsticks.
239:Nom, nom, nom... Eh, this familiar nose-scrunching feeling is from mustard?
240:Yes, my mother says that kale is only nice when it's drizzled with a mixture of soy sauce and mustard.
241:Which means the yellow thing on this fried pork cutlet is also... yes, it's also yellow mustard. Ahem, sorry, but can you pass me the water again...
242:I look at the bento box and realize that every food item in it, including the dessert, is spicy in its own way. Even the tender white rice tastes faintly of pickled peppers, which makes me completely speechless for a while. Hmm... can a spicy dessert still be called a dessert...?
243:...Nana, do you love eating spicy things?
244:That's right. Me and my whole family like eating spicy foods, but the food I've made today is a little mild because I'm worried that you can't eat food that's too spicy.
245:Mild... Can I try a bite of yours?
246:I suspect that Nana Shiraishi prepared my bento box as a prank, but after tasting hers, I have to honestly admit that I'm just too weak to enjoy the delicious bento box in front of me, which she regards as being mildly flavored.
247:Jack's Voice
248:Jill, you make such delicious food. What will I do if I get spoiled by your cooking?
249:While I'm drinking water to relieve the spiciness, I hear Jack praising Jill's cooking behind me, so I turn to look enviously at the delicacies they are eating.
250:After that, an incredible scene enters my eyes.
251:It's so delicious... I can't stop eating. You need to make less food next time, or else I'll get fat and won't look handsome anymore.
252:Oh, you always know what to say. Eat as much as you like.
253:Before I even start to comment on the indescribable food that is releasing purple bubbles in the bento box, I want to say that food shouldn't make you look livid and pop your eyes out no matter how delicious it is, right?!
254:But even so, the happy smile on Jack's face at this moment is genuine. This... I guess this is the power of love.
255:When I turn my gaze away from that chaotic yet sweet scene and look back at the bento box in my hand, I can't help but imagine Nana Shiraishi bustling about while she prepared these bento boxes. Under her gentle smile that melts into the sunshine, I feel ashamed of my earlier cowardice.
256:(whisper) It's just a little spicy. It's not a big deal. Nana worked hard to prepare this, so I must eat everything...
257:...Hmm? {var:player_nickname}, your forehead is covered in sweat. Is the food too spicy for you?
258:No way! This is mildly seasoned, so it isn't spicy at all. I'll be okay. Sweating is good for the body.
259:Mmm-mmm, delicious! You're so thoughtful, you know? It's been getting colder recently, so it's a perfect time to eat spicy food. *coughs*
260:A-Are you okay?
261:I'm okay... The food is just too delicious, haha... so I ended up eating too quickly. I'll be okay after drinking some water.
262:Are you sure you're okay? Your face is completely red now. You don't need to force yourself to eat everything if it's too spicy for you.
263:No!
264:Keep eating! Don't stop! These tears I'm shedding after eating this food are proof of my happiness! What I have in my hands isn't just a simple bento box. It represents love! LOVE! What I need to respond to this love is... the courage to rise to the occasion and take the bull by the horns!
265:(whisper) Don't be scared. No matter how spicy it is, at least... at least it shouldn't kill me!
266:When I stand up with swollen lips to clean the bento box, Jack also stands up with a pale face. His eyes seem a little dilated, but he is still smiling happily.
267:Yo... my friend, have you finished your bento box...?
268:Of course... I ate everything...
269:My friend, you deserve this.
270:Jack gives me a thumbs up, and I smile back at him in response. Life sure is amazing. After eating one meal, the man in front of me and I suddenly appreciate each other like old friends. As I support his trembling body, I hope that I won't need to call an ambulance later...
271:After having lunch and passing the test of love with my and Jack's lives on the line, the four of us stroll around while we think about where to go next.
272:(whisper) Nana, it would be best to go to sing karaoke or something. If we walk around on the streets for too long, there's a high chance that we'll meet an acquaintance and get found out.
273:(whisper) You're right. Let's do that.
274:Jill, shall we go to sing karaoke?
275:Okay, but I just saw a fortune-telling stall and want to have my fortune told first.
276:...I have a bad feeling about this.
277:Kaavi
278:Welcome.
279:Is there only one fortune-telling stall in One Han City?!
280:(whisper) Wh-What should we do?! Will Kaavi expose us?
281:(whisper) D-Don't panic yet. She doesn't know that we're pretending to be a couple, so let's just not ask her to tell our fortunes...
282:Hello, we want to ask you about our love fortune. Nana, would you also like to have your fortune told too?
283:N-No, I'll be fine...
284:That won't do. The future is so unpredictable. The more you know in advance, the more you can do to protect your relationship! We're here anyway, so let's both have our fortunes told.
285:A couple...
286:Kaavi looks at Nana Shiraishi and me, making us both feel frightened under her gaze. Fortunately, she doesn't really say anything. Instead, she lowers her head and fiddles with the tarot cards on the table as she starts telling Jill's fortune.
287:...The Lovers is upright, which means that your romance will become more intimate. This is a good sign.
288:You drew The Lovers card when asking about your love fortune. You've got good luck, Jill.
289:How can you call it luck when it's destiny. It's your turn now, Nana.
290:Okay...
291:After seeing Nana Shiraishi and I sit down, Kaavi puts away the tarot cards and places a crystal ball in the center of the table.
292:Why aren't you using tarot cards this time?
293:It's important to use the right fortune-telling method for each person to reveal the right answer that destiny has in store for them. Please wait quietly for your fortune to be told.
294:...Oh, this is interesting.
295:Wh-What can you see?
296:I can sense the rapport and intimacy that you two share... I can see your present, but I can't see a shred of your future because a layer of fog is obscuring my vision. It's been a while since destiny has eluded me like this.
297:Does this mean that Nana's relationship won't go well? Can you try to tell their fortune again?
298:It's rude to forcefully tear off the veil of fate, but... I can take some steps to actively approach it.
299:...What advice can you give us?
300:This is an amulet my master gave to me, and I've kept it at home for a long time now, but I suddenly thought of taking it with me today for some reason. Now that I think about it, maybe it wants to find a more suitable owner for itself.
301:Okay, I'll buy it. How much does it cost?
302:Its price will be determined by the one who is hungry for answers.
303:After all that, it turns out that what she wants is money... Since Kaavi didn't expose us right away, I paid her some hush money, which was about double what I paid her for an amulet the last time.
304:Hehe... nice doing business with you.
305:Huh? Sorry, I need to take a phone call.
306:Hello... Huh? Right now? Sorry, I don't think I can come right now...
307:What is it?
308:Please wait a moment... My friend in the swimming club said they need one more person for their training match and asked if I can help out... It doesn't matter though. I'll get them to ask someone else.
309:You should go since they are waiting for you.
310:But aren't we on a date? It's not good to just leave you here like this.
311:Just go, or else you'll keep worrying about whether they managed to find anyone and won't enjoy yourself anyway. We'll continue our date another day.
312:I guess you're right... I'll listen to you then. I'm sorry, Jill! I need to go to school right now. I'll buy you a drink another day.
313:Just go. It's not like you haven't suddenly left us while we're out before.
314:Even if she is helping others out, it's still kinda insensitive of her to leave halfway through a date. Aren't you angry at all?
315:It's alright. I'm already used to it. She has such an enthusiastic personality, and that's also what makes her so likable.
316:Wow, that's so thoughtful. Although it's good to be considerate of your girlfriend, {var:player_nickname}, you don't have to be so understanding all the time.
317:Haha, then would it be better if I acted jealous?
318:A lover who gets jealous is cuter. By the way, if you don't chase after her and cheer for her, all that effort you two put into pretending to be a couple today would be in vain.
319:She knows? This is bad. I wonder what gave it away. What should I do now...?
320:Admit it directly
321:Don't give anything away
322:...How did you find out?
323:Oh? You're not going to try to explain?
324:Since you brought this up, I'm sure you've noticed something that doesn't add up. There's no point trying to say anything otherwise now.
325:Well, instead of saying that I noticed anything, it's more like Nana just sucks at acting. She was so embarrassed that her ears were completely red when you held her hand at the beginning. If you really are dating, there's no way she would get that embarrassed, right?
326:Okay then... but is that the only thing that gave us away?
327:{var:player_nickname}, you acted really natural, but you also gave it away when we were having lunch. Even a classmate like me knows that Nana makes really spicy food, so if you really are her boyfriend, you wouldn't have been taken by surprise by her spicy food.
328:But this act wouldn't have been possible if she didn't bring you with her today. To be honest, you've done really well already. If you had left and gone to school with her just then, I might have thought that you two had just started dating and ignored the things that seemed strange to me.
329:While it's true that couples don't need to go everywhere together, there's no reason why you wouldn't leave with her in this situation. I mean, you wouldn't be intentionally staying here to be our third wheel, right?
330:...Sigh, I got careless. I guess it is indeed unnatural to let your own girlfriend leave alone while you stay with another couple. What's worse is that I just met you today, so it's even weirder for me to stay here.
331:Why didn't you expose us earlier if you noticed that we were just pretending?
332:Because it's amusing, of course. Hahaha, it's really fun to see you and Nana rushing around trying to trick us.
333:Oh... by the way, it's kinda of my fault that you had to spend so much on that amulet. Let me pay for half of it.
334:No, you don't need to. Think of it as my just deserts for trying to trick you.
335:Let's just walk around randomly for a little longer and then go to pick Nana up from the school together later. Even if you're just pretending to be a couple, it's still true that you're on a date, and it would be too sad for your girlfriend to have to go home all alone at this time.
336:You're right. I'll take this advice from a real couple to heart.
337:Let's go then. By the way, why haven't you said anything this entire time, Jack? Why are you in a daze?
338:...{var:player_nickname}, so you and Nana aren't really dating?!
339:...He's a slow idiot. Just ignore him.
340:He actually admitted he was tricked by me, which made my efforts seem somewhat worthwhile. I really want to cry now.
341:My friend, you deserve this.
342:...Hmm? Jill, why have you come?
343:I came especially with your guy to pick you up. Shouldn't you run up and give your boyfriend a big hug?
344:O-Of course I'm happy, but I don't think it's necessary to hug him...
345:Jill, you can stop teasing her now. Nana, we don't need to pretend anymore.
346:Eh... I'm sorry, Jill! I didn't mean to trick you. I did this because...
347:You don't need to apologize to me. We had lots of fun today, didn't we? As for your reason for doing this, {var:player_nickname} already told me when we were on our way here.
348:I'm sorry, Nana. I'll stop introducing guys to you.
349:Really?
350:You should have just told me directly if I was making you feel uncomfortable. Or did you think I would get angry at you? If I knew you already had someone so nice as a potential boyfriend, I wouldn't have tried so hard to introduce you to guys.
351:Are you talking about {var:player_nickname}?
352:Huh?!
353:Who else? Think about it. Most people would get angry if their date left them during a date, let alone support their willful desire to help others.
354:I think {var:player_nickname} is quite a nice person. You two should just start dating for real.
355:J-Junior, don't listen to what Jill is saying. She's just joking!
356:Whether I'm joking or not depends on how things develop between you two. Well, we'll be off now. You two can take your time and have a good chat.
357:...Oh, by the way, Nana, have you already thought of an explanation?
358:An explanation? Don't you already know the truth?
359:I do, but what about everyone else? One Han City is both big and small. Are you really that confident... that we were not seen by anyone we know today?
361:Several days later
362:Hahaha... this is such a coincidence. I'm also trying to think of my response to a bunch of text messages filled with question marks...
363:As we speak, my phone vibrates again on the table, and I have even less courage to reply to the message when I see that the sender is Ren Kisaragi...
364:Pretending to be a couple... Nana and me? I'm sorry, I don't understand what you're saying.
365:I didn't say I wouldn't go and cheer for her. I was just about to go.
366:Really? Then why didn't you leave with her just now?
367:I stayed behind to buy her some sports drinks and other things.
368:You're more considerate than I expected. In that case, give Nana my regards.
369:I leave quickly in case I give anything else away and sigh in relief under my breath after making sure that Jack and Jill are no longer behind me. Jill's sudden probe really gave me a fright just now.
370:I wonder what gave us away... Is it because I didn't leave with Nana? That would make sense. If I really am going out with Nana, it is a little weird to let her go to school alone while I stay and hang out with two people I barely know.
371:Oh, there she is.
372:They are resting at halftime when I arrive at the school with water and protein bars. At this moment, Nana Shiraishi is sitting next to the pool and wiping herself with a towel.
373:How did it go today?
374:Eh?! J-Junior, why are you here?
375:I've come to cheer for you.
376:Swimming Club Member A
377:Nana, who is this?
378:Swimming Club Member B
379:He's even brought water and food. This enthusiasm... He can't be here just to cheer for you, right?
380:Swimming Club Member C
381:Junior... Oh, I know! Isn't this the person who Nana is always talking about?
382:Don't listen to them! I'm not always talking about... Hmm?! Hmm!!!
383:Nana, please stay quiet until we finish asking all our questions. I've got her under control. Ask the questions now!
384:Hello, how did you and Nana meet?
385:Let's get directly to the point. What's your relationship with Nana?
386:What's my relationship with her? She's my senpai, and I'm her junior.
387:Is that all?
388:You... stop a-asking all these random questions!
389:...Nana loves to help people, and she takes care of many of her juniors. I'm one of them.
390:But I think I'm more special than the others because she once said that I'm her "most trustworthy junior."
391:She's also my most trustworthy and important senpai.
392:J-Junior...
393:Are you happy with this answer?
394:Your most important senpai...
395:Yes! This answer leaves a lot to the imagination. I'm happy with it!
396:I'll get out of your way now.
397:Hey! Don't leave so quickly! Come back! Our relationship isn't what you think...
398:They are all very far away now, so you can stop shouting. Are you hungry? Do you want something to eat?
399:Thanks... but you shouldn't humor them. You don't have to tell them anything.
400:They are going to let their imagination run wild even if I don't say anything. I just gave them an answer they can accept so they will stop disturbing your rest.
401:We're the only people who need to know what relationship we have. Also, I meant what I said. They can interpret my words however they like.
402:I guess you're right... By the way, you didn't come here just to cheer for me, right? Did Jill say something?
403:She started suspecting that we aren't really going out because I didn't leave with you, so I rushed over here.
404:But I think this isn't the only thing that made her suspect us. You should start thinking of what you should say to her.
405:Well... if all else fails, I can just apologize to her and admit that I was lying to her...
406:I'm sorry. I left without thinking too much about it and let you clean up after me.
407:It's not the first time you've acted this recklessly, so I'm already used to it.
408:You don't have to put it so bluntly... Now that I think about it, someone like me is no good in a relationship. Who would like a girlfriend who would abandon them at the drop of a hat to help someone else?
409:It's a good thing that we aren't really dating, or else even someone with a good temper like you would get angry at me.
410:I can't say for sure. When you like someone, you're usually attracted by their strengths, and isn't your love of helping others part of your charm? I think that if I fall in love with you, I'll definitely be prepared to accept this willful part of you.
411:Junior... Well, you know that I'm quite reckless sometimes. Don't you think it's troublesome to get involved in all sorts of weird things by someone like me?
412:Of course it's troublesome. My legs were sore for days after Orio chased us around.
413:I-I'm sorry... I should have massaged your legs for longer if I knew you would be sore for so long...
414:Although it's troublesome, it's also really fun. If life wasn't so fulfilling and meaningful with you, do you think I would accompany you everywhere?
415:So wipe that sad look off your face now. It's not like you at all to keep worrying about this and that.
416:Hmm... Hehe, now that I think about it, I still have hope...
417:What hope?
418:N-Nothing! I mean... umm... if Jill asks us out on another double date, you'll be willing to help me out again, right?
419:Again... Umm, yes.
420:I can't help it since this troublesome senpai is my most important senpai. I have to keep my word, right?
421:What should we do?! When we were dating, Hana, Ransei, Eliisa, and... in short, a lot of people saw us holding hands while walking around! When I was cleaning the playground, they gathered around me and kept asking me about it. What should I say to them?!{var:Shake}
427:Hmm... you're probably right. If you really are in a relationship, there's no way I, the president of the love committee, wouldn't have noticed.
